course: dictionary
lesson: 15796
title: Unanswered and the prefix un-
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Break the word into two parts: un- and answered. The prefix un- means not, so unanswered means not answered. «Mia asked three questions, but two were left unanswered.» Those two questions got no reply.
explain: Use the same check as before: swap your meaning into the sentence. «The teacher read out the unanswered questions, then waited.» If you put "not answered" in place of "unanswered", the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: The word can also describe a call, text or challenge that nobody responded to. «Dad's phone showed an unanswered call from Grandma» means the phone rang and nobody picked up. Look for clue words such as question, call or prayer.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so «unanswered» means not answered or not replied to.
fact: «Unanswered» is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in «an unanswered question».
fact: Useful phrases are «left unanswered» and «an unanswered call».
fact: In a test, an unanswered question gets no marks. In stories and science, unanswered questions are mysteries still to solve.
exercise: «The question on the board was left unanswered.» What does unanswered mean here? | *Not answered | Answered very well | Asked twice | Written in pencil
exercise: Find the word in this sentence that means not answered: «Her unanswered text sat on the screen all day.» | *unanswered | all | screen | text
exercise: What does the prefix un- mean in unanswered? | Before | Again | Very | *Not
test: Which phrase means a phone call that nobody picked up? | A call from the teacher | A loud call | A call home for tea | *An unanswered call
test: Which word is the opposite of answered? | Asked | *Unanswered | Written | Replied
exam: Which sentence uses unanswered correctly? | The bell was unanswered loudly | Unanswered, the children sang | *The question stayed unanswered all lesson | The unanswered dog ran home fast
